# nr-office-quality-trust: what the lead applies (all of it is in files this task does not own)

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-quality/src/lib.rs
Add, in the `pub mod` block in alphabetical place (after `pub mod checklist;` and before `pub mod issue;`, the
trust module last after `pub mod score;`):

    pub mod document_brief;
    pub mod document_design_review;
    pub mod trust;

(`document_brief` and `document_design_review` go right after `pub mod document_acceptance;`; `trust` after `pub mod score;`.)
The crate doc comment may add: "the prompt-injection analysis of external documents with the mutation gate
(`trust`), the document brief and the native document design review".

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-quality/Cargo.toml
[dependencies], add (workspace crates already in the lock, both already workspace members and dependencies):

    mixdog-fsio = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-ooxml = { workspace = true }

[dev-dependencies], add:

    base64 = { workspace = true }
    tempfile = { workspace = true }
    # The document-brief tests and the twin test answer the BriefReadings of document_brief with the authoring crate's
    # brief parser. A dev-dependency cycle (mixdog-office-author depends on this crate for `issue_with`) is allowed by
    # Cargo; the tests are integration tests, so both sides link the same library build of this crate.
    mixdog-office-author = { workspace = true }

No new crate enters Cargo.lock (mixdog-fsio, mixdog-ooxml, mixdog-office-author, base64 and tempfile are in it);
only the dependency edges of mixdog-office-quality change. mixdog-office-author must be a workspace member
(nr-office-author-brief's wire).

## 3. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json
Run `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs --write-index` once the wave is merged: it adds the row of
the new set `office-trust` (recorder benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-trust.mjs, 1 file, golden.json). The
set's own MANIFEST.json is already written (native/core/fixtures/office-trust/MANIFEST.json).

## 4. Consumers (later tasks of the track, not this one)
- trust: `trust::{analyze_office_prompt_injection, analyze_office_file_prompt_injection, combine_office_trust_reviews,
  assert_office_mutation_allowed}`. The office tools that open an external document call the analysis, put the report
  in their answer as `trust`, and call `assert_office_mutation_allowed(Some(&trust), acknowledgeUntrustedContent === true)`
  before a mutation (Err carries Node's refusal text). The file analysis takes a `ReadProof` (the caller's lane token).
- document_brief: `BriefReadings` is the seam to the brief parser of `mixdog-office-author` (which depends on this
  crate, so this crate cannot call it). The caller that holds both (the docx/xlsx/pdf office tool) defines one unit
  struct whose four methods call `mixdog_office_author::brief::{html_brief_script, parse_authoring_brief,
  review_fact_coverage, review_source_grounding}` (see tests/common/mod.rs for the exact four lines) and passes it to
  `document_brief(readings, text)` and `document_brief_issues(readings, format, document, brief)`.
- document_design_review: `review_native_document_design(format, issues)` takes the issues of the structure review.
  nr-office-quality-structure adds the one-line call `review_native_document_design(format,
  review_office_structure(format, document, audit_profile))` beside its `structure` module; the wording and the
  `ok`/`status`/`modelReview` shape are here.

## 5. Findings for the owners of other files (not changed here)
- mixdog-ooxml zipio.rs `no_end_of_central_directory`: for a file that does not begin as a zip jszip 3.10.2 says
  "Can't find end of central directory : is this a zip file ? If it is, see https://stuk.github.io/jszip/documentation/howto/read_zip.html";
  the Rust text stops after "directory". The trust analysis passes the text to the user as a warning, so a garbage
  file named .docx shows the shorter text. (A truncated real zip, "Corrupted zip: can't find end of central
  directory", is equal; the twin recording covers that case and not the garbage one for this reason.)
- mixdog-ooxml package.rs `os_message` is pub(crate); trust.rs reaches its text through `load_package`'s failed read.
  Making it pub would let `read_failure` in trust.rs call it directly.

## 6. Nothing else
No protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING name, no desktop fragment, no environment variable.
